# Implementation: Show how many tasks are left

Taiga #10 · reads `docs/spec.md`, `docs/design.md`

## Scope

Frontend-only, exactly as designed. No backend changes.

## Files changed

- **New:** `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx` — presentational component,
  takes `open`/`done` integer props, renders one `<p className="task-counts"
  role="status">` with independent singular/plural grammar per bucket, per
  `docs/design.md`'s spec verbatim.
- **`frontend/src/App.jsx`:**
  - Import `TaskCounts` (line 3, alphabetical with the other component
    imports).
  - `openCount = tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length` added next to the
    existing `completedCount` (line 39-40) — both derive from `tasks`, never
    `visibleTasks`/`sortedTasks`.
  - `{!loading && <TaskCounts open={openCount} done={completedCount} />}`
    rendered directly under `<h1>Tasks</h1>` (line 56), above `AddTask`.
- **`frontend/src/App.css`:**
  - `h1` bottom margin tightened from `1.2rem` to `0.3rem` so the counts line
    sits snug under the title.
  - New `.task-counts` rule added next to `.empty, .loading` (same "muted
    secondary text" category): `margin: 0 0 1.2rem; font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #5a646c;` — the AA-contrast-passing color computed in
    `docs/design.md` (5.63:1 on the page background), not a reuse of the
    existing `#6b7780` (which the design doc found fails at 4.28:1).

No other files touched. `frontend/src/api.js` untouched — no new request.

## Deviations from design

None. Component shape, wiring, CSS, and placement all match `docs/design.md`
verbatim.

## Verification

- **Build:** `cd frontend && npm run build` — succeeds, no errors:
  ```
  ✓ 22 modules transformed.
  ✓ built in 109ms
  ```
- **Tests:** `cd frontend && npm test` — fails with `npm error Missing
  script: "test"`. This is a **pre-existing gap**, not introduced by this
  change: `frontend/package.json` has no `test` script and no testing
  library (`@testing-library/react`, `vitest`, etc.) is installed anywhere in
  the repo (`node_modules/.bin/` only has `oxlint`, `vite`, `rolldown`,
  `nanoid`). There is no existing frontend test to use as a precedent for
  this component, and installing a test framework is out of scope for a
  single-component feature diff per the "minimal diff" discipline — flagging
  for reviewer/product-manager rather than silently skipping.
- **Lint:** not run — `oxlint` is not in this session's Bash allowlist
  (`.claude/settings.json` permits `npm run build*`/`npm run dev*`/`npm
  test*` but not `npm run lint*`, and direct `node_modules/.bin/oxlint`
  invocation is likewise outside the allowlist). Reviewer has broader Bash
  access and should run `npm run lint` to confirm.
- **Manual/visual check:** not run (no browser tool in this dispatch's
  toolset). Reviewer's pass should exercise: zero tasks, exactly one task in
  each bucket, add/complete/delete/clear-completed transitions, loading
  state (count absent), and error state (count keeps last-known values) —
  matching the states enumerated in `docs/design.md`.

## How to run and verify

```bash
cd backend  && python3 -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload   # terminal 1
cd frontend && npm run dev                                 # terminal 2
```
Open the app: the counts line reads e.g. "3 tasks open · 2 tasks done"
under the "Tasks" heading, updates immediately on add/complete/delete/clear
completed with no reload, and disappears only during the initial load.

## Known limitations

- No automated test coverage for `TaskCounts` or the new `openCount`
  derivation — see "Tests" above. The logic is a one-line pure filter
  (`tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length`), directly parallel to the
  already-untested `completedCount` on the line above it, so this follows
  existing project precedent rather than introducing a new gap in test
  discipline.
```

